// expect: refuse E_EffectUnhandled
// AN INSTALL SOMEWHERE IS CREDITED FOR A PERFORM IT DOES NOT COVER. The same
// body as mn-refuse-sibling-mask with the declaration taken off: the left
// operand performs E under `~> h`, the right operand performs E through a
// second HOF call no install encloses, and nothing declares a row. E reaches
// main's root row — the row is right — and the executable gate clears it
// because `h` is installed somewhere in the program.
//
// MEASURED 2026-09-23 through the current wheel: zero diagnostics, an
// executable emitted, and the run faults out of bounds in ev_declaring_node
// — the uncovered op reading evidence no install threaded. So nothing
// executes unproven is false here, and not even the walk's own belt fires:
// the fault is a memory access, not the named trap.
//
// The credit is deliberate and measured (report_unhandled_names in
// pipeline.mn): deleting it refuses the wheel, whose nested graph installs
// forward sibling GraphRead ops through an outer install the row cannot see.
// Telling that forwarding apart from this uncovered site is install identity
// — a performed name discharged by an install that REACHES it — and this
// fixture holds the refusal until the gate reads the install chain
// (Hβ.effects.reachable-perform-with-no-install-compiles).
effect E { op() -> Int }

handler h {
  op() => resume(1),
}

fn run(f) = f()

fn run2(g) = g()

fn bad() = ((run(() => op())) ~> h) + run2(() => op())

fn main() = bad()
